        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. The Fatah party elects new central commitee for the first time in 10 years Middle East Issued on: 14/05/2026 - 15:37 The Fatah party is due to elect its new central committee for the first time in 10 years. It comes as questions arise over whether President Mahmoud Abbas will finally step aside after more than two decades at the helm. Major figures from within the movement are boycotting the vote and accusing the leadership of usurping power. Story by Delano D’Souza. Lebanese split over diplomatic normalisation amid Washington talks 14/05/2026 Middle East Israel-Lebanon ceasefire nears end: Will fresh talks lead to new truce? 14/05/2026 Middle East Did Israel tip Eurovision 2025 results? NYT report delves into voting data 14/05/2026 Middle East Netanyahu's coalition seeks to dissolve parliament and trigger early election in Israel 14/05/2026 Middle East Israel launches fresh strikes on Lebanon despite ceasifre and ongoing talks 14/05/2026 Middle East ‘Divide and rule’: Mahmoud Abbas keeps Fatah 'divided', ensuring no potential successor can emerge 14/05/2026 Middle East Price shocks from Iran war power solar sales in energy-hungry Asia 13/05/2026 Middle East Hamas committed 'systematic' sexual violence during October 7 attacks, says report 12/05/2026 Middle East Israel passes law establishing military tribunal for October 7 perpetrators 12/05/2026 Middle East"
