        "orario": "15:31",
        "timestamp": 1778765469,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Xi-Trump diplomacy: Beijing envisions 4 pillars of 'stability', warns US over Taiwan 'interference' Access Asia Issued on: 14/05/2026 - 15:31 Modified: 14/05/2026 - 15:38 Donald Trump is the first US leader to visit Beijing in nearly a decade. Amid the pomp, circumstance and high-level meetings, Angela Diffley welcomes Shanhui ZHANG, Journalist at CGTN (China Global Television Network) and Fellow at the Center for China and Globalisation. From the outset, Zhang frames the relationship in almost symbolic and ritual terms, suggesting that “when the two top leaders are talking together, that’s how we can decide the future of the China and the U.S. relations.” The discussion unfolds around two distinct leadership dynamics and how they intersect with contested geopolitical issues such as Taiwan, Ukraine and the Middle East. Beijing sees itself as a world-class mediator and “responsible power that looks like what a power should be in the 21st century.” Aung San Suu Kyi moved to house arrest 01/05/2026 Access Asia Notion of women as property a 'depravity baked into law', expert says 29/01/2026 Access Asia China's top general under investigation 24/01/2026 china 01/01/2026 china Taiwan: Chinese military releases footage of drills around the island 29/12/2025 china Thailand's PM sets course for early election amid border and parliamentary unrest 12/12/2025 Access Asia Cambodia retaliates in renewed clashes with Thailand as death toll mounts to 10 09/12/2025 Access Asia Xi holds his ground as Macron's visit to China only yields modest returns 05/12/2025 Asia / Pacific China warns citizens against Japan travel as Taiwan spat escalates 17/11/2025 china"
